#   1. Fill every <PLACEHOLDER> below with the real value (KIT_SHA,
#      BUILD_RUN_ID, GATE_A_RUN_ID, SHA256_SETUP_EXE, Valid/NotSigned), and
#      resolve the "<IF T4 PASSED ...>" conditional sentence -- delete it if
#      T4 did not measure real packets.
#   2. Apply with `git apply docs/releases/beta4-truth.patch` (verified to
#      apply cleanly against this branch's docs/releases/release-truth.yaml
#      with `git apply --check`), or edit the file by hand to match.
#   3. Update docs/releases/2026-09-03-beta4-release-notes.md and
#      docs/releases/v1.0.0-beta.4-verification.md with the same real values
#      and the same conditional resolution.
#   4. Update README.md's "Current version" banner, INSTALL-WINDOWS.md,
#      docs/tester/lpm-beta-test-handoff.md, and docs/tester/START-HERE.md to
#      name v1.0.0-beta.4 as current and v1.0.0-beta.3 as superseded (they
#      currently still name beta.3 as current and beta.4 as the next/held
#      candidate, matching the still-staging manifest this patch changes).
#   5. Give CHANGELOG.md's "## [Unreleased]" section a
#      "## [1.0.0-beta.4] - <RELEASE_DATE>" heading (keep a fresh, empty
#      "## [Unreleased]" above it) -- required by
#      scripts/policy/check_release_identity.py once README no longer marks
#      beta.4 as an "owner-held unpublished candidate".
#   6. Run `scripts/policy/check_release_truth.py --live --readme README.md`
#      and `scripts/policy/check_release_identity.py`; both must PASS before
#      publishing.
#
